    "expectTitle": "Framing — \"but is not limited to\"",
    "script": "Learning objectives\n\nBy the end of this hour, participants will be able to:\n\n1. Distinguish the function of O.C.G.A. 43-10A-17 from that of Board Rule Chapter 135-7.\n2. Describe the scope of the catch-all disciplinary ground at 43-10A-17(a)(6), including its lack of an injury requirement.\n3. Identify the circumstances under which privilege does not protect licensee or client records in a board proceeding.\n4. Apply the textual tension between 135-7-.03(2)(c) and 135-7-.01(2)(m) to a multi-client record request.\n\nTiming. 5 min framing · 15 min statute · 25 min Case A · 15 min documentation close.\n\n1. Framing (5 min)\n\nEvery rule in Chapter 135-7 reads the same way: a principle, then *\"unprofessional conduct includes, but is not limited to,\"* followed by an enumerated list.\n\nNovice clinicians learn the list. Experienced clinicians practice in the space that phrase opens — conduct that is disciplinable and appears nowhere in the chapter.\n\nThis hour establishes two things. Where the board's authority actually comes from, and what happens when two provisions of the same chapter point opposite directions."
