    "script": "5. Close (5 min)\n\nThree things from this hour worth carrying:\n\nCompetence under (e) is measured by training received, not by outcomes achieved or years accumulated. Almost everyone in the room has drift, and drift is disciplinable whether or not it is disciplined.\n\nUnder (g) and (i), the arrangements most likely to create exposure are the ones that arrived as ordinary business practice rather than as a decision.\n\nAnd the rule is not the outer boundary. 43-10A-17 reaches further on impairment, on competence, and on conduct generally. Reading Chapter 135-7 alone gives a licensee a smaller picture of their exposure than the one the board is working from."
