    "expectTitle": "Close",
    "script": "4. Close (5 min)\n\nThree points.\n\nInstitutional cover is not a thing the rule recognizes. Rule .04(1) says it in the first sentence, and licensees rarely read past the enumerated list to find it.\n\nThe duty under (d) is triggered by awareness and is narrower than instinct. It requires forthright evaluation and appropriate recommendations to the supervisee. That is a real duty, discharged in the supervision relationship, and it is not the same as reporting. But 43-10A-17(a)(7) sits behind it, and it reaches knowingly aiding unlicensed or unlawful practice.\n\nYour supervision record is reachable. Under 43-10A-17(h)(1) and (c), board investigators have access to any material relating to a licensee's fitness, backed by subpoena. Supervisors document defensively for the supervisee's benefit and rarely consider that the same document describes what the supervisor knew and when.\n\nFinal exercise, 3 min individually: Write the supervision note for the first disclosure in Case D — the one that happens before you know anything else. Three sentences.\n\nThen read one aloud. The gap between what people wrote and what they'd want on record two years later is the hour."
