    "script": "Hour 5 — Advertising, assessment, and data\n\nLearning objectives\n\nBy the end of this hour, participants will be able to:\n\n1. Evaluate professional marketing materials against the four enumerated standards at 135-7-.07(2).\n2. Revise noncompliant marketing copy into copy that satisfies 135-7-.07 while still serving its commercial purpose.\n3. Apply the standards at 135-7-.07(2) to the participant's own professional materials.\n4. Describe the affirmative duty to correct misrepresentations made by third parties.\n5. Identify business entity naming restrictions under Chapter 135-10.\n6. Apply the assessment standards at 135-7-.05(2)(b) and (d) to an instrument used outside its norming population.\n7. Assess whether platform or vendor data use satisfies the informed consent standard at 135-7-.06(2)(c).\n\nTiming. 3 min open · 31 min advertising · 14 min assessment · 12 min research and data.\n\nPlacement note. This is the last hour and attention is spent. The advertising block is competitive and runs on the room's energy rather than yours. Keep it first.\n\n1. Open (3 min)\n\nAsk how many people in the room have read Chapter 135-7.\n\nThen tell them there are thirteen chapters, and that at least three others govern conduct they engage in daily — Chapter 135-10 on advertising, Chapter 135-11 on telemental health, Chapter 135-12 on testing and assessment. A licensee who has read only the code of ethics has read one chapter of thirteen."
